::SQL Inner Join::
Which of the following statements are correct?
{
    ~Inner-joins are the least frequent types of joins
    ~SQL joins can't produce valid output if there are common columns and values on 2 or more tables
    ~Inner-joins are opposite of Equijoins.
    =In SQL joins, Inner JOIN is one of the most commonly used JOIN. 
}

::SQL Inner Join::
What is the output of the following SQL statement?
SELECT Orders.orderId, Orders.totalamount, Customers.customerID, Customers.f_name, Customers.L_Name
FROM Orders, customers 
WHERE customers.customerID = orders.customerid;
{
    ~A list of all employee IDs and their First_name and Last_name
    =A list of all the customers and their order amounts
    ~A list of matching employee IDs and their First_name and Last_name
    ~None of the above
}



